rfc894.txt, rfc1112.txt, rfc2464.txt, rfc7042.txt
    The texts of RFC 894 (IP Datagrams over Ethernet Networks), RFC 1112 (Host Extensions for IP
    Multicasting), RFC 2464 (Transmission of IPv6 Packets over Ethernet Networks) and RFC 7042 (IANA
    Considerations and IETF Protocol and Documentation Usage for IEEE 802 Parameters), downloaded from
    https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/ on 2026-10-26.
    License: the IETF Trust's Legal Provisions Relating to IETF Documents.
    Used: the multicast mappings of RFC 1112 §6.4 and RFC 2464 §7, the interface identifier example of
    RFC 2464 §4, and the EtherTypes of RFC 7042.

linux.txt
    Frames that the Linux kernel (7.0.14-linuxkit, of Docker Desktop on arm64, with the tools of Debian
    trixie) sent between two network namespaces joined by a veth pair, captured with tcpdump on 2026-10-26:
    ARP, NDP and MLDv2, ICMP and ICMPv6 echoes of 3,000 bytes (fragmented at an MTU of 1,500), an echo with
    the Record Route option, frames with an 802.1Q tag and with 802.1ad and 802.1Q tags, and UDP and TCP
    exchanges over IPv4 and IPv6. Checksum offloading was turned off, so that every checksum is the kernel's.
    Each frame is a line of hexadecimal after "# " lines with tcpdump's summary of it (`tcpdump -n -e -v`).
    Made by linux.sh, run as `docker run --rm --privileged -v "$PWD":/out debian:trixie sh /out/linux.sh`,
    and `python3 linux.py capture.pcap capture.txt linux.txt` on its output.
    License: produced for this project (no third-party content).
